# Presence answers do not settle the timing decision

Document ID: `reiyah.observation-contract.report`.
Version: `0.1.0`.
Lifecycle status: `exploratory`.
Date: 20 September 2026.

**All 623 unresolved partial-timing operating cases retain opposing decisions
even when every unknown instance is present and eligible in both worlds.**
The complete presence answers and object counts agree. Their geometries differ.
This is a checked development result under the inherited optional-box contract,
not a measurement of actual cars or a product-performance advantage.

The [frozen plan](PLAN.md) selected every unresolved current/union partial row
before new constructions. Parent outcomes were already known. No threshold,
prediction, membership, known reference, census, eligibility rule, loss or
universal bound changed. The [complete table](results.csv) retains all 623
dependent cases; [summary.json](summary.json) binds the publication artifacts.

| Allocation or check | Result |
| --- | ---: |
| Primary / diagnostic-anchor rows | 444 / 179 |
| Current / union partial-timing rows | 529 / 94 |
| Distinct filtered states / state-family pairs | 542 / 689 |
| Distinct completion jobs and new native proofs | 803 |
