These counts overlap and are not independent trials. Zero is non-improvement;
every paired upper endpoint is strictly positive. Across the unchanged 7,707
parent rows, 642 remain supported, 3,076 excluded, 1,790 unresolved and 2,199
input-blocked. The other 1,167 unresolved rows are one-edit cases outside this
construction. All parent identities and decisions are exact-bound to their
retained verification; only the 623 allocated cases are newly recomposed here.

The [construction](METHOD.md) adds an eligible reference with no matching edge
for each absent unknown identity. Maximum matching ranks and paired loss stay
unchanged. Positive width has no declared minimum, so a sufficiently narrow
rectangle supplies such a reference. This reveals the breadth of the model:
the constructed narrow boxes are not asserted to be plausible physical cars.

The inference is specific: **presence/count questions cannot guarantee a
decision for every world in this contract**. It is not a claim that every
possible presence transcript is ambiguous. A real absent answer could rule
out these witnesses. A justified geometry, motion or shape observation could
also narrow the world set; imposing a convenient constraint after seeing the
result would not validate that constraint.

The separate [checker](check.py) imports no new completion producer. It
checks geometry and identity, recomputes matching through augmenting paths,
checks all 803 native proof payloads and recomposes all case means.
[Verification](verification.json) is same-session internal checking, not
independent scientific replication. Twenty-two authored controls include 58
finite optional worlds; four frozen-input and two actual-result binding
forgeries are rejected. Three supervisor controls verify unfinished-command
rejection, cumulative-budget rejection and network denial before execution.

Run the authored controls from the repository root with an existing Python
environment containing the Engine's pinned dependencies (including jsonschema):

```sh
python -B research/observation-contract/0.1.0/test_contract.py /tmp/reiyah-observation-controls.json
```

The output path must be new. Empirical replay requires the exact private source
custody named by the freeze; those restricted operands and proofs are not shipped.
No new dependency download or model execution was used for this study.

Construction used 9.049285416 outer-process seconds; actual checking used
10.829932458, plus 3.287873791 for actual-result rejection controls. Cumulative
limits were 600 seconds per category. [Costs](COSTS.md) distinguish these
timers from elapsed time and unknown engineering/human/economic costs.
A preparation path collision was corrected before the freeze with exact bytes
retained privately; no private payload was staged or published. All negative
findings and historical failures remain discoverable.

The [primary-source review](SOURCES.md) supports checking decision
identifiability before optimizing query order. A 2026 sensing-clock preprint
adds current context but supplies no measurement validity or Reiyah advantage.
This elementary observation is not presented as a new frontier theorem.

Next technical gate: qualify an observation that can distinguish decision
classes, or justify a narrower residual geometry model with external evidence,
then freeze a matched comparison. For a genuine value test, the missing record
is an actual consequential revision decision and its complete observation and
work costs. For example: a team's successive detector builds evaluated on the
same permitted scenes, with time logged for resolving disputed references and
an explicit rule for deciding whether to integrate the new build. No such
private team records are asserted available. Their absence does not block
independent useful technical or public-source work.

